# .public-surface-deny - denials this repository adds on top of the fleet baseline.
#
#     category | path-glob | reason | pattern
#
# The allowlist lets this repository name its secrets tool in prose and in deploy
# tooling. That mask must not extend to the tool's own configuration file, which
# names the recipients a store is encrypted to, so it is denied again here under
# a category of its own that the allowlist does not touch.

secret-store-config | * | an encrypted secret store and its creation-rules file never belong in a public repository, whatever the surrounding documentation is allowed to say | (^|/)\.%73ops\.ya?ml($|[^a-z0-9])
